1:["$","$Ld",null,{"active":"01-neural-networks","title":"第 1 讲 · 人工神经网络基础","children":["$","$Le","01-neural-networks",{"lesson":{"slug":"01-neural-networks","number":1,"title":"人工神经网络基础","english":"Fundamentals of Artificial Neural Networks","shortTitle":"人工神经网络基础","topics":["引言与概览","多层感知机","神经网络训练","案例分析"],"topicAnchors":["topic-1","topic-31","topic-66","topic-129"],"pages":165,"hidden":15,"summary":"从识别芒果的例子开始，理解神经元、网络层、前向传播与反向传播，再讨论优化、正则化和真实案例。"},"content":{"file":"1.Fundamentals of Artificial Neural Networks.pptx","slides":[{"page":1,"part":"ppt/slides/slide1.xml","text":["Fundamentals of ANNs","(2026)","Lecturer: Xue Yang","yangxue.site"],"pictures":4,"hidden":false,"media":[],"links":[],"figure":{"page":1,"kind":"roadmap","title":"人工神经网络基础","caption":"从任务定义到训练，再走向完整工程流程","note":"","url":"/diagrams/1/1.svg","sourceElements":[]}},{"page":2,"part":"ppt/slides/slide2.xml","text":["Contents","Introduction & Overview","Multi-Layer Perceptron","﻿Training Neural Networks","Case Analysis"],"pictures":3,"hidden":false,"media":[],"links":[],"figure":{"page":2,"kind":"roadmap","title":"人工神经网络基础","caption":"从任务定义到训练，再走向完整工程流程","note":"","url":"/diagrams/1/2.svg","sourceElements":[]}},{"page":3,"part":"ppt/slides/slide3.xml","text":["Introduction & Overview","Mango Selection","How can you tell if it's a mango?","How can you tell if a mango is sweet?"],"pictures":1,"hidden":false,"media":[],"links":[],"figure":{"page":3,"kind":"classification","title":"从特征到预测","caption":"数据提供示例，模型学习输入与类别之间的映射","note":"训练样本 → 参数学习 → 新样本预测","url":"/diagrams/1/3.svg","sourceElements":[{"url":"/diagrams/elements/1/image7.png","lesson":1,"page":3}]}},{"page":4,"part":"ppt/slides/slide4.xml","text":["Introduction & Overview","Mango","Apple","Mango","Apple"],"pictures":22,"hidden":false,"media":[],"links":[],"figure":{"page":4,"kind":"classification-compare","title":"人工特征与自动学习表示","caption":"传统机器学习与深度学习的处理流程","note":"训练样本 → 参数学习 → 新样本预测","url":"/diagrams/1/4.svg","sourceElements":[{"url":"/diagrams/elements/1/image8.png","lesson":1,"page":4,"crop":[0.014,0.146,0.12,0.233]}]}},{"page":5,"part":"ppt/slides/slide5.xml","text":["前向传播","反向传播","损失函数","真实标签","预测结果","迭代训练","优化器","权重","Introduction & Overview"],"pictures":1,"hidden":false,"media":[],"links":[],"figure":{"page":5,"kind":"training","title":"从预测误差到参数更新","caption":"前向产生预测，反向计算梯度，优化器更新参数","note":"训练样本 → 参数学习 → 新样本预测","url":"/diagrams/1/5.svg","sourceElements":[]}},{"page":6,"part":"ppt/slides/slide6.xml","text":["Introduction & Overview","Origin: Artificial Intelligence","In recent years, AI has become the biggest winner of the Nobel Prize/Turing Award. As an irresistible force, it is driving a paradigm shift in scientific research.","Turing Award, 2018/2024"],"pictures":4,"hidden":false,"media":[],"links":[],"figure":{"page":6,"kind":"timeline","title":"人工智能的发展线索","caption":"从可计算的智能问题，到由数据驱动的模型","note":"不同阶段的方法相互联系，并非简单替代。","url":"/diagrams/1/6.svg","sourceElements":[]}},{"page":7,"part":"ppt/slides/slide7.xml","text":["Introduction & Overview","Origin: Artificial Intelligence","生物制药","自动驾驶","人形机器人","大模型"],"pictures":6,"hidden":true,"media":[{"url":"/materials/1/media/image31.GIF","type":"animation"}],"links":[],"figure":{"page":7,"kind":"timeline","title":"人工智能的发展线索","caption":"从可计算的智能问题，到由数据驱动的模型","note":"不同阶段的方法相互联系，并非简单替代。","url":"/diagrams/1/7.svg","sourceElements":[]}},{"page":8,"part":"ppt/slides/slide8.xml","text":["Introduction & Overview","Origin: Artificial Intelligence","生物制药","自动驾驶","人形机器人","大模型"],"pictures":6,"hidden":false,"media":[{"url":"/materials/1/media/image31.GIF","type":"animation"}],"links":[],"figure":{"page":8,"kind":"timeline","title":"人工智能的发展线索","caption":"从可计算的智能问题，到由数据驱动的模型","note":"不同阶段的方法相互联系，并非简单替代。","url":"/diagrams/1/8.svg","sourceElements":[]}},{"page":9,"part":"ppt/slides/slide9.xml","text":["Introduction & Overview","Origin: Artificial Intelligence","Alan Turing (1912-1954)","1931 Admitted to King's College, Cambridge, with a scholarship in mathematics.","1938 Earned his PhD from the Institute for Advanced Study at Princeton, USA.","1939 Called up to work for the British Foreign Office, cracking enemy codes.","1945 Awarded the highest government honor, the Order of the British Empire.","1954 Died by suicide."],"pictures":2,"hidden":false,"media":[],"links":[],"figure":{"page":9,"kind":"timeline","title":"人工智能的发展线索","caption":"从可计算的智能问题，到由数据驱动的模型","note":"不同阶段的方法相互联系，并非简单替代。","url":"/diagrams/1/9.svg","sourceElements":[]}},{"page":10,"part":"ppt/slides/slide10.xml","text":["Introduction & Overview","Origin: Artificial Intelligence","The Turing Test (1950s)","Separate humans from machines.","Humans ask questions via electronic communication devices.","After multiple rounds of Q&A, if over 30% of people can't distinguish whether the respondent is human or machine, the machine passes the test and is considered to possess human-level intelligence."],"pictures":1,"hidden":false,"media":[],"links":[],"figure":{"page":10,"kind":"timeline","title":"人工智能的发展线索","caption":"从可计算的智能问题，到由数据驱动的模型","note":"不同阶段的方法相互联系，并非简单替代。","url":"/diagrams/1/10.svg","sourceElements":[]}},{"page":11,"part":"ppt/slides/slide11.xml","text":["Introduction & Overview","A和B哪个更像人类的回答？为什么？","问：你会下国际象棋吗？","答：是的。","问：你会下国际象棋吗？","答：是的，我不是已经说过了吗？","问：你会下国际象棋吗？","答：你烦不烦，干嘛老是提同样的问题。","A","B","问：你会下国际象棋吗？","答：是的。","问：你会下国际象棋吗？","答：是的。","问：你会下国际象棋吗？","答：是的。"],"pictures":1,"hidden":false,"media":[],"links":[],"figure":{"page":11,"kind":"searchtree","title":"博弈中的决策","caption":"从当前状态展开候选行动，再比较后续结果","note":"搜索树表示可能的决策路径，图中的分支为机制示意。","url":"/diagrams/1/11.svg","sourceElements":[]}},{"page":12,"part":"ppt/slides/slide12.xml","text":["Introduction & Overview","A和B哪个更像人类的回答？为什么？","问：你会下国际象棋吗？","答：是的。","问：你会下国际象棋吗？","答：是的，我不是已经说过了吗？","问：你会下国际象棋吗？","答：你烦不烦，干嘛老是提同样的问题。","A","B","问：你会下国际象棋吗？","答：是的。","问：你会下国际象棋吗？","答：是的。","问：你会下国际象棋吗？","答：是的。","遵照特定规则回答","机械式回答","具有综合分析和理解的能力","能探知提问者在反复提出相同的问题"],"pictures":1,"hidden":false,"media":[],"links":[],"figure":{"page":12,"kind":"searchtree","title":"博弈中的决策","caption":"从当前状态展开候选行动，再比较后续结果","note":"搜索树表示可能的决策路径，图中的分支为机制示意。","url":"/diagrams/1/12.svg","sourceElements":[]}},{"page":13,"part":"ppt/slides/slide13.xml","text":["Introduction & Overview","表达多样化","内容死板","当今的大模型是否具备人类智能呢？","是的，我可以帮助你了解国际象棋的规则、策略和技巧。如果你有任何具体的问题或者想讨论某个棋局，随时告诉我!","是的，我可以帮助你理解国际象棋的规则、策略和战术。如果你想讨论某个棋局、学习开局或了解特定的战术，请告诉我!"],"pictures":5,"hidden":false,"media":[],"links":[],"figure":{"page":13,"kind":"generation","title":"从输入到生成结果","caption":"根据已有上下文，逐步构造响应","note":"可观察的任务表现与能力适用范围需要分别讨论。","url":"/diagrams/1/13.svg","sourceElements":[]}},{"page":14,"part":"ppt/slides/slide14.xml","text":["Introduction & Overview","一个有趣的实验","弱人工智能","强人工智能","通用智能","认知 & 理解","学习 & 推理"],"pictures":5,"hidden":false,"media":[{"url":"/materials/1/media/media1.mp4","type":"video"}],"links":[],"figure":{"page":14,"kind":"generation","title":"从输入到生成结果","caption":"根据已有上下文，逐步构造响应","note":"可观察的任务表现与能力适用范围需要分别讨论。","url":"/diagrams/1/14.svg","sourceElements":[]}},{"page":15,"part":"ppt/slides/slide15.xml","text":["Introduction & Overview","人工智能的主要流派","深度学习","神经机器翻译","机器阅读理解","预训练LLM","符号主义","符号表达，数理逻辑推理","规则系统、专家系统","联结主义","模拟人脑神经元的连接方式","Yann LeCun：LeNet","Geoffrey Hinton：BP、DBN","Yoshua Bengio：GAN","深度学习之父"," 2018年图灵奖","兴起","图灵测试","熵&信息论","马尔可夫过程","香农、图灵","乔姆斯基生成文法","感知机、特征工程","知识图谱"],"pictures":7,"hidden":false,"media":[],"links":[],"figure":{"page":15,"kind":"branches","title":"人工智能的三种研究路线","caption":"用不同的建模假设组织知识、学习与行为","note":"","url":"/diagrams/1/15.svg","sourceElements":[]}},{"page":16,"part":"ppt/slides/slide16.xml","text":["Introduction & Overview","Artificial Intelligence → Deep Learning","The differences and connections between AI and DL"],"pictures":2,"hidden":false,"media":[],"links":[],"figure":{"page":16,"kind":"nested","title":"人工智能、机器学习与深度学习","caption":"理解研究范围之间的包含关系","note":"深度学习属于机器学习；人工智能还包含其他研究方法。","url":"/diagrams/1/16.svg","sourceElements":[]}},{"page":17,"part":"ppt/slides/slide17.xml","text":["Introduction & Overview","Artificial Intelligence → Deep Learning","Broad ","Concept","Practical ","Techniques","Making computers work like humans","Uses algorithms to analyze data, learn from it, and measure or predict real-world events","A specific implementation technology","Deep","Learning","Machine","Learning","Artificial ","Intelligence"],"pictures":7,"hidden":false,"media":[],"links":[],"figure":{"page":17,"kind":"nested","title":"人工智能、机器学习与深度学习","caption":"理解研究范围之间的包含关系","note":"深度学习属于机器学习；人工智能还包含其他研究方法。","url":"/diagrams/1/17.svg","sourceElements":[]}},{"page":18,"part":"ppt/slides/slide18.xml","text":["Introduction & Overview","Artificial Intelligence → Deep Learning","Artificial Intelligence","Machine Learning","Deep Learning","Providing methods for implementing artificial intelligence","Providing technology for implementing machine learning"],"pictures":1,"hidden":false,"media":[],"links":[],"figure":{"page":18,"kind":"nested","title":"人工智能、机器学习与深度学习","caption":"理解研究范围之间的包含关系","note":"深度学习属于机器学习；人工智能还包含其他研究方法。","url":"/diagrams/1/18.svg","sourceElements":[]}},{"page":19,"part":"ppt/slides/slide19.xml","text":["Introduction & Overview","The Development of Deep Learning","When a neuron is \"excited,\" it sends chemicals to connected neurons, altering their electrical potential.","If the potential exceeds a threshold (𝜃), the neuron is activated."," Learned knowledge is embedded in the connection weights (𝜔) and threshold (𝜃).","Future","Budding","1943","M-P Neuron Model","[McCulloch and Pitts,  1943]","Activation Function"],"pictures":1,"hidden":false,"media":[],"links":[],"figure":{"page":19,"kind":"timeline","title":"神经网络发展的共同条件","caption":"模型、数据、计算与训练方法相互促进","note":"","url":"/diagrams/1/19.svg","sourceElements":[]}},{"page":20,"part":"ppt/slides/slide20.xml","text":["Introduction & Overview","The Development of Deep Learning","Future","Budding","1943","Boom Period","Perceptron (1958), Adaline (1960), Perceptrons (1969)","The ideal activation function is the step function:","0: Inhibits the neuron","1: Activates the neuron","The step function is discontinuous and non-smooth.","Commonly used alternative: Sigmoid function"],"pictures":1,"hidden":false,"media":[],"links":[],"figure":{"page":20,"kind":"timeline","title":"神经网络发展的共同条件","caption":"模型、数据、计算与训练方法相互促进","note":"","url":"/diagrams/1/20.svg","sourceElements":[]}},{"page":21,"part":"ppt/slides/slide21.xml","text":["Introduction & Overview","Artificial Intelligence → Deep Learning","First Winter (1976-1982), faced skepticism due to ","Insufficient computing power, ","High computational complexity, ","Great implementation difficulty","Future","Budding","1943","Boom Period","Perceptron (1958), Adaline (1960), Perceptrons (1969)","AI Winter"],"pictures":0,"hidden":false,"media":[],"links":[],"figure":{"page":21,"kind":"nested","title":"由人工智能到深度学习","caption":"将本课程的模型原理放在更大的研究范围中","note":"","url":"/diagrams/1/21.svg","sourceElements":[]}},{"page":22,"part":"ppt/slides/slide22.xml","text":["Introduction & Overview","The Development of Deep Learning","A neural network is a widely interconnected network of adaptive simple units.","Its organization can simulate the interaction responses of biological nervous systems to real-world objects. [T. Kohonen, NN88]","Solving general learning problems","Integrated with biological systems","Future","Budding","1943","Boom Period","Perceptron (1958), Adaline (1960), Perceptrons (1969)","Neural Network","1986","Nature","AI Winter"],"pictures":2,"hidden":false,"media":[],"links":[],"figure":{"page":22,"kind":"timeline","title":"深度学习的发展脉络","caption":"从网络结构到可训练、可扩展的模型","note":"","url":"/diagrams/1/22.svg","sourceElements":[]}},{"page":23,"part":"ppt/slides/slide23.xml","text":["Introduction & Overview","The Development of Deep Learning","Future","Budding","1943","Boom Period","Perceptron (1958), Adaline (1960), Perceptrons (1969)","Neural Network","1986","Nature","AI Winter"],"pictures":5,"hidden":false,"media":[],"links":[],"figure":{"page":23,"kind":"timeline","title":"深度学习的发展脉络","caption":"从网络结构到可训练、可扩展的模型","note":"","url":"/diagrams/1/23.svg","sourceElements":[]}},{"page":24,"part":"ppt/slides/slide24.xml","text":["Introduction & Overview","The Development of Deep Learning","Future","Budding","1943","Boom Period","Perceptron (1958), Adaline (1960), Perceptrons (1969)","Neural Network","1986","Nature","AI Winter","High training difficulty","Insufficient computational power of computers","Limited training data volume","Poor performance"],"pictures":3,"hidden":false,"media":[],"links":[],"figure":{"page":24,"kind":"timeline","title":"深度学习的发展脉络","caption":"从网络结构到可训练、可扩展的模型","note":"","url":"/diagrams/1/24.svg","sourceElements":[]}},{"page":25,"part":"ppt/slides/slide25.xml","text":["Introduction & Overview","The Development of Deep Learning","Future","Budding","1943","Boom Period","Perceptron (1958), Adaline (1960), Perceptrons (1969)","Neural Network","1986","Nature","AI Winter","Better model design","Greater computer computing power","Large-scale database collection","Significant performance improvement","Big data + increased model complexity","Silent Period","Tradition ML Models (SVM, Boosting, …)","Deep Belief Network","2006","Science"],"pictures":2,"hidden":false,"media":[],"links":[],"figure":{"page":25,"kind":"timeline","title":"深度学习的发展脉络","caption":"从网络结构到可训练、可扩展的模型","note":"","url":"/diagrams/1/25.svg","sourceElements":[]}},{"page":26,"part":"ppt/slides/slide26.xml","text":["Introduction & Overview","The Development of Deep Learning","Future","Budding","1943","Boom Period","Perceptron (1958), Adaline (1960), Perceptrons (1969)","Neural Network","1986","Nature","AI Winter","Silent Period","Tradition ML Models (SVM, Boosting, …)","Deep Belief ","Network","2006","Science","2012","Explosion Age","Rank","Institute","Error rate","Description","1","U. Toronto","0.15315","Deep Learning","2","U. Tokyo","0.26172","Hand‐crafted features and learning models.","Bottleneck.","3","U. Oxford","0.26979","4","Xerox/INRIA ","0.27058","Comparison of object recognition effects","(1,000,000 images and 1,000 categories)"],"pictures":4,"hidden":false,"media":[],"links":[],"figure":{"page":26,"kind":"timeline","title":"深度学习的发展脉络","caption":"从网络结构到可训练、可扩展的模型","note":"","url":"/diagrams/1/26.svg","sourceElements":[]}},{"page":27,"part":"ppt/slides/slide27.xml","text":["Introduction & Overview","Future","Budding","1943","Boom Period","Perceptron (1958), Adaline (1960), Perceptrons (1969)","Neural Network","1986","Nature","AI Winter","Silent Period","Tradition ML Models (SVM, Boosting, …)","Deep Belief ","Network","2006","Science","2012","Explosion Age","AlexNet, the beginning of deep learning","2012","Seq2Seq, sequence generation network","2014","2018","BERT, bidirectional transformer","GPT-1, the first generation of large models","ResNet, residual solution extends network depth","2015","2019","GPT-2","2020","GPT-3","Transformer, reform of the attention mechanism NLP model","2017","2022"," DALL-E2","2021"," DALL-E, test-to-image","2014","GANs","2021","CLIP, Multimodal retrieval model","OpenAI o1","2024","2023","GPT-4, DALL-E3","Stable Diffusion XL","2024","Stable Diffusion 3","GPT-4o, Support multimodality","2022","ChatGPT, Human-computer dialogue","Stable Diffusion, Text-Image Diffusion Model","Deep thinking","2025","2015","2020"],"pictures":12,"hidden":false,"media":[],"links":[],"figure":{"page":27,"kind":"branches","title":"把人工智能能力连接到实际任务","caption":"应用目标决定数据、模型与评价方法","note":"","url":"/diagrams/1/27.svg","sourceElements":[]}},{"page":28,"part":"ppt/slides/slide28.xml","text":["Introduction & Overview","Future","Budding","1943","Boom Period","Perceptron (1958), Adaline (1960), Perceptrons (1969)","Neural Network","1986","Nature","AI Winter","Silent Period","Tradition ML Models (SVM, Boosting, …)","Deep Belief ","Network","2006","Science","2012","Explosion Age","New algorithm design patterns","Domain Knowledge","Key factors for success: Big data + new learning models"],"pictures":5,"hidden":false,"media":[],"links":[],"figure":{"page":28,"kind":"branches","title":"把人工智能能力连接到实际任务","caption":"应用目标决定数据、模型与评价方法","note":"","url":"/diagrams/1/28.svg","sourceElements":[]}},{"page":29,"part":"ppt/slides/slide29.xml","text":["Introduction & Overview","Future","Budding","1943","Boom Period","Perceptron (1958), Adaline (1960), Perceptrons (1969)","Neural Network","1986","Nature","AI Winter","Silent Period","Tradition ML Models (SVM, Boosting, …)","Deep Belief ","Network","2006","Science","2012","Explosion Age","Key factors for success: Big data + new learning models","Development direction"],"pictures":4,"hidden":false,"media":[],"links":[],"figure":{"page":29,"kind":"branches","title":"把人工智能能力连接到实际任务","caption":"应用目标决定数据、模型与评价方法","note":"","url":"/diagrams/1/29.svg","sourceElements":[]}},{"page":30,"part":"ppt/slides/slide30.xml","text":["Introduction & Overview","Future","Budding","1943","Boom Period","Perceptron (1958), Adaline (1960), Perceptrons (1969)","Neural Network","1986","Nature","AI Winter","Silent Period","Tradition ML Models (SVM, Boosting, …)","Deep Belief ","Network","2006","Science","2012","Explosion Age","Feature learning","Jointly optimize the \"feature transformer + classifier\" approach","Leverage computer-generated learning of feature representations","Better leverage big data","Quickly acquire features suitable for new applications","96 learned low‐level filters"],"pictures":4,"hidden":false,"media":[],"links":[],"figure":{"page":30,"kind":"branches","title":"把人工智能能力连接到实际任务","caption":"应用目标决定数据、模型与评价方法","note":"","url":"/diagrams/1/30.svg","sourceElements":[]}},{"page":31,"part":"ppt/slides/slide31.xml","text":["Contents","Introduction & Overview","Multi-Layer Perceptron","﻿Training Neural Networks","Case Analysis"],"pictures":3,"hidden":false,"media":[],"links":[],"figure":{"page":31,"kind":"roadmap","title":"多层感知机","caption":"由局部运算组成可学习的非线性函数","note":"","url":"/diagrams/1/31.svg","sourceElements":[]}},{"page":32,"part":"ppt/slides/slide32.xml","text":["Multi-Layer Perceptron","Modeling One Neuron","Biological (left) vs. artificial neuron analogy (right)"],"pictures":1,"hidden":false,"media":[],"links":[],"figure":{"page":32,"kind":"neuron","title":"单个神经元的计算","caption":"对输入加权求和，再施加激活函数","note":"权重控制各输入的作用，偏置调整响应位置。","url":"/diagrams/1/32.svg","sourceElements":[]}},{"page":33,"part":"ppt/slides/slide33.xml","text":["Multi-Layer Perceptron","Single Neuron Analogy","output of -th neuron analogy :","Nonlinear Activation","Linear combiation","Weight","Bias"],"pictures":1,"hidden":false,"media":[],"links":[],"figure":{"page":33,"kind":"neuron","title":"单个神经元的计算","caption":"对输入加权求和，再施加激活函数","note":"权重控制各输入的作用，偏置调整响应位置。","url":"/diagrams/1/33.svg","sourceElements":[]}},{"page":34,"part":"ppt/slides/slide34.xml","text":["Multi-Layer Perceptron","Single Neuron as a Linear Classifier","Input: 𝑥 ∈ ℝ𝐷","Output: 𝑊𝑥 + 𝑏 = 𝑓(𝑥) ∈ ℝ𝐶","Learnable Parameters: 𝑊 ∈ 𝑅𝐶×𝐷, 𝑏 ∈ ℝ𝐶"],"pictures":3,"hidden":false,"media":[],"links":[],"figure":{"page":34,"kind":"linear","title":"线性层与分类分数","caption":"矩阵的一行对应一个输出单元","note":"先检查输入维度、输出维度与参数矩阵的形状。","url":"/diagrams/1/34.svg","sourceElements":[]}},{"page":35,"part":"ppt/slides/slide35.xml","text":["Multi-Layer Perceptron","Single Neurons stack → Neural Network Layer","Output stack","Output Vector ","Input Vector","Weight Matrix"],"pictures":1,"hidden":false,"media":[],"links":[],"figure":{"page":35,"kind":"linear","title":"线性层与分类分数","caption":"矩阵的一行对应一个输出单元","note":"先检查输入维度、输出维度与参数矩阵的形状。","url":"/diagrams/1/35.svg","sourceElements":[]}},{"page":36,"part":"ppt/slides/slide36.xml","text":["Multi-Layer Perceptron","A Linear Classifier Example","Example for 2x2 image, 3 classes (cat/dog/ship)"],"pictures":1,"hidden":false,"media":[],"links":[],"figure":{"page":36,"kind":"linear","title":"线性层与分类分数","caption":"矩阵的一行对应一个输出单元","note":"先检查输入维度、输出维度与参数矩阵的形状。","url":"/diagrams/1/36.svg","sourceElements":[]}},{"page":37,"part":"ppt/slides/slide37.xml","text":["Multi-Layer Perceptron","A Linear Classifier Example","Interpreting an linear classifier: Algebraic viewpoint"],"pictures":1,"hidden":true,"media":[],"links":[],"figure":{"page":37,"kind":"linear","title":"线性层与分类分数","caption":"矩阵的一行对应一个输出单元","note":"先检查输入维度、输出维度与参数矩阵的形状。","url":"/diagrams/1/37.svg","sourceElements":[]}},{"page":38,"part":"ppt/slides/slide38.xml","text":["Multi-Layer Perceptron","A Linear Classifier Example","Interpreting an linear classifier: Algebraic viewpoint"],"pictures":1,"hidden":true,"media":[],"links":[],"figure":{"page":38,"kind":"linear","title":"线性层与分类分数","caption":"矩阵的一行对应一个输出单元","note":"先检查输入维度、输出维度与参数矩阵的形状。","url":"/diagrams/1/38.svg","sourceElements":[]}},{"page":39,"part":"ppt/slides/slide39.xml","text":["Multi-Layer Perceptron","A Linear Classifier Example","Interpreting an linear classifier: Algebraic viewpoint"],"pictures":1,"hidden":true,"media":[],"links":[],"figure":{"page":39,"kind":"linear","title":"线性层与分类分数","caption":"矩阵的一行对应一个输出单元","note":"先检查输入维度、输出维度与参数矩阵的形状。","url":"/diagrams/1/39.svg","sourceElements":[]}},{"page":40,"part":"ppt/slides/slide40.xml","text":["Multi-Layer Perceptron","A Linear Classifier Example","Interpreting an linear classifier: Geometric viewpoint"],"pictures":5,"hidden":true,"media":[],"links":[],"figure":{"page":40,"kind":"linear","title":"线性层与分类分数","caption":"矩阵的一行对应一个输出单元","note":"先检查输入维度、输出维度与参数矩阵的形状。","url":"/diagrams/1/40.svg","sourceElements":[]}},{"page":41,"part":"ppt/slides/slide41.xml","text":["Multi-Layer Perceptron","Hard Cases for a Linear Classifier","A single neuron cannot solve many problems!","Solution: Multi-Layer Perceptron (MLP w/ activation functions)","Famous XOR problem: No linear separator exists!"],"pictures":3,"hidden":false,"media":[],"links":[],"figure":{"page":41,"kind":"decision","title":"线性边界的表达局限","caption":"有些类别分布无法由一个超平面分开","note":"异或分布为示意数据，用于说明非线性表示的必要性。","url":"/diagrams/1/41.svg","sourceElements":[]}},{"page":42,"part":"ppt/slides/slide42.xml","text":["Multi-Layer Perceptron","2-layer Neural Networks","Input: 𝑥 ∈ ℝ𝐷","Output: 𝑊2𝑚𝑎𝑥 (0, 𝑊1𝑥 + 𝑏1)\t+ 𝑏2 = 𝑓(𝑥) ∈ ℝ𝐶","Learnable Parameters: 𝑊1 ∈ ℝ𝐻×𝐷, 𝑊2 ∈ ℝ𝐶×𝐻, 𝑏1 ∈ ℝ𝐻, 𝑏2 ∈ ℝ𝐶"],"pictures":1,"hidden":false,"media":[],"links":[],"figure":{"page":42,"kind":"network","title":"隐藏层与深层网络","caption":"通过多层变换构造新的特征表示","note":"相邻层之间的连接对应可学习权重。","url":"/diagrams/1/42.svg","sourceElements":[]}},{"page":43,"part":"ppt/slides/slide43.xml","text":["Multi-Layer Perceptron","2-layer Neural Networks","Input: 𝑥 ∈ ℝ𝐷","Output: 𝑊2𝑚𝑎𝑥 (0, 𝑊1𝑥 + 𝑏1)\t+ 𝑏2 = 𝑓(𝑥) ∈ ℝ𝐶","Learnable Parameters: 𝑊1 ∈ ℝ𝐻×𝐷, 𝑊2 ∈ ℝ𝐶×𝐻, 𝑏1 ∈ ℝ𝐻, 𝑏2 ∈ ℝ𝐶","Element (i, j) of  gives the effect on  from  ","Element (j, k) of  gives the effect on  from  "],"pictures":1,"hidden":false,"media":[],"links":[],"figure":{"page":43,"kind":"network","title":"隐藏层与深层网络","caption":"通过多层变换构造新的特征表示","note":"相邻层之间的连接对应可学习权重。","url":"/diagrams/1/43.svg","sourceElements":[]}},{"page":44,"part":"ppt/slides/slide44.xml","text":["Multi-Layer Perceptron","2-layer Neural Networks","Input: 𝑥 ∈ ℝ𝐷","Output: 𝑊2𝑚𝑎𝑥 (0, 𝑊1𝑥 + 𝑏1)\t+ 𝑏2 = 𝑓(𝑥) ∈ ℝ𝐶","Learnable Parameters: 𝑊1 ∈ ℝ𝐻×𝐷, 𝑊2 ∈ ℝ𝐶×𝐻, 𝑏1 ∈ ℝ𝐻, 𝑏2 ∈ ℝ𝐶","Element (i, j) of  gives the effect on  from  ","Element (j, k) of  gives the effect on  from  ","All elements of  affect all elements ","All elements of  affect all elements "],"pictures":1,"hidden":false,"media":[],"links":[],"figure":{"page":44,"kind":"network","title":"隐藏层与深层网络","caption":"通过多层变换构造新的特征表示","note":"相邻层之间的连接对应可学习权重。","url":"/diagrams/1/44.svg","sourceElements":[]}},{"page":45,"part":"ppt/slides/slide45.xml","text":["Multi-Layer Perceptron","Deep Neural Networks","Input: 𝑥 ∈ ℝ𝐷","Output: 𝑓(𝑥) ∈ ℝ𝐶","Learnable Parameters: 𝑊1, … 𝑊6, 𝑏1, … 𝑏6"],"pictures":1,"hidden":false,"media":[],"links":[],"figure":{"page":45,"kind":"network","title":"隐藏层与深层网络","caption":"通过多层变换构造新的特征表示","note":"相邻层之间的连接对应可学习权重。","url":"/diagrams/1/45.svg","sourceElements":[]}},{"page":46,"part":"ppt/slides/slide46.xml","text":["Multi-Layer Perceptron","Deep Neural Networks","Setting number of layers and their sizes","overfitting","generalization"],"pictures":1,"hidden":false,"media":[],"links":[],"figure":{"page":46,"kind":"network","title":"隐藏层与深层网络","caption":"通过多层变换构造新的特征表示","note":"相邻层之间的连接对应可学习权重。","url":"/diagrams/1/46.svg","sourceElements":[]}},{"page":47,"part":"ppt/slides/slide47.xml","text":["Multi-Layer Perceptron","Deep Neural Networks Example"],"pictures":1,"hidden":true,"media":[],"links":[],"figure":{"page":47,"kind":"forward","title":"沿网络完成一次前向传播","caption":"每一层的输出成为下一层的输入","note":"","url":"/diagrams/1/47.svg","sourceElements":[]}},{"page":48,"part":"ppt/slides/slide48.xml","text":["Multi-Layer Perceptron","Activation Functions","Why activation functions?"],"pictures":1,"hidden":false,"media":[],"links":[],"figure":{"page":48,"kind":"composition","title":"为什么不能只堆叠线性层","caption":"连续的线性变换仍可以合并为一次线性变换","note":"表达能力的关键变化来自中间的非线性。","url":"/diagrams/1/48.svg","sourceElements":[]}},{"page":49,"part":"ppt/slides/slide49.xml","text":["Multi-Layer Perceptron","Activation Functions","Suppose we remove all activation functions former layer output :","current layer output  :","while "],"pictures":1,"hidden":false,"media":[],"links":[],"figure":{"page":49,"kind":"composition","title":"为什么不能只堆叠线性层","caption":"连续的线性变换仍可以合并为一次线性变换","note":"表达能力的关键变化来自中间的非线性。","url":"/diagrams/1/49.svg","sourceElements":[]}},{"page":50,"part":"ppt/slides/slide50.xml","text":["Multi-Layer Perceptron","Activation Functions","Degradation ","Conclusion: The linear superposition property makes stacking multiple linear layers meaningless, as they can always be reduced to a single layer.","Activation functions are necessary !"],"pictures":0,"hidden":false,"media":[],"links":[],"figure":{"page":50,"kind":"composition","title":"为什么不能只堆叠线性层","caption":"连续的线性变换仍可以合并为一次线性变换","note":"表达能力的关键变化来自中间的非线性。","url":"/diagrams/1/50.svg","sourceElements":[]}},{"page":51,"part":"ppt/slides/slide51.xml","text":["Multi-Layer Perceptron","Activation Functions","Input: 𝑥 ∈ ℝ𝐷","Output: 𝑊2𝑚𝑎𝑥 (0, 𝑊1𝑥 + 𝑏1)\t+ 𝑏2 = 𝑓(𝑥) ∈ ℝ𝐶","The function 𝑅𝑒𝐿𝑈(𝑧) = max(0, 𝑧) is called “Rectified Linear Unit”"],"pictures":1,"hidden":false,"media":[],"links":[],"figure":{"page":51,"kind":"activation","title":"ReLU 与 Leaky ReLU","caption":"比较正负区间的响应与梯度","note":"Leaky ReLU 的负区间斜率在图中取 0.1，仅作示意。","url":"/diagrams/1/51.svg","sourceElements":[]}},{"page":52,"part":"ppt/slides/slide52.xml","text":["Multi-Layer Perceptron","Activation Functions","Pros and Cons to using the ReLUs:","Sparsity: Zero output for negative inputs promotes network sparsity and generalization.","Mitigates Vanishing Gradients: Gradient is exactly 1 in the positive region, preventing decay in deep networks.","Dying ReLU Problem: Neurons can get \"stuck\" outputting 0, making gradients permanently zero."],"pictures":0,"hidden":false,"media":[],"links":[],"figure":{"page":52,"kind":"activation","title":"ReLU 与 Leaky ReLU","caption":"比较正负区间的响应与梯度","note":"Leaky ReLU 的负区间斜率在图中取 0.1，仅作示意。","url":"/diagrams/1/52.svg","sourceElements":[]}},{"page":53,"part":"ppt/slides/slide53.xml","text":["Multi-Layer Perceptron","Activation Functions","Leaky ReLU: Leaky ReLUs are one attempt to fix the “dying ReLU” problem.","Adds a small slope to negative inputs to prevent \"death\""],"pictures":2,"hidden":false,"media":[],"links":[],"figure":{"page":53,"kind":"activation","title":"ReLU 与 Leaky ReLU","caption":"比较正负区间的响应与梯度","note":"Leaky ReLU 的负区间斜率在图中取 0.1，仅作示意。","url":"/diagrams/1/53.svg","sourceElements":[]}},{"page":54,"part":"ppt/slides/slide54.xml","text":["Multi-Layer Perceptron","Activation Functions","Sigmoid:","Sigmoids saturate and kill gradients. When the neuron’s activation saturates at either tail of 0 or 1, the gradient at these regions is almost zero"],"pictures":1,"hidden":false,"media":[],"links":[],"figure":{"page":54,"kind":"activation","title":"Sigmoid 与饱和区间","caption":"当输入绝对值很大时，输出变化逐渐减小","note":"二分类输出与隐藏层激活的选择需要区别对待。","url":"/diagrams/1/54.svg","sourceElements":[]}},{"page":55,"part":"ppt/slides/slide55.xml","text":["Multi-Layer Perceptron","Activation Functions","Pros and Cons to using the Sigmoid:","Probabilistic Interpretation: Directly outputs values (0, 1) interpretable as probabilities, so it’s ideal for for binary classification.","Smooth Gradient: Differentiable everywhere, enabling gradient-based optimization.","Vanishing Gradients: Gradients ≈ 0 for extreme inputs (｜𝑥｜≫ 0), stalling learning in deep networks."],"pictures":0,"hidden":false,"media":[],"links":[],"figure":{"page":55,"kind":"activation","title":"Sigmoid 与饱和区间","caption":"当输入绝对值很大时，输出变化逐渐减小","note":"二分类输出与隐藏层激活的选择需要区别对待。","url":"/diagrams/1/55.svg","sourceElements":[]}},{"page":56,"part":"ppt/slides/slide56.xml","text":["Multi-Layer Perceptron","Activation Functions","Softmax:","The sum is 1."],"pictures":1,"hidden":false,"media":[],"links":[],"figure":{"page":56,"kind":"softmax","title":"从分数得到类别分布","caption":"指数变换后按总和归一化","note":"计算示例使用分数 [1, 2, 3]，输出概率之和为 1。","url":"/diagrams/1/56.svg","sourceElements":[]}},{"page":57,"part":"ppt/slides/slide57.xml","text":["Multi-Layer Perceptron","Activation Functions","Pros and Cons to using the Softmax:","Probabilistic Interpretation: The output directly represents the probability of a sample belonging to each class, making it suitable for multi-class classification tasks.","Gradient Behavior: The derivative involves interactions between the probabilities of different classes, enabling efficient gradient computation during back propagation."],"pictures":0,"hidden":false,"media":[],"links":[],"figure":{"page":57,"kind":"softmax","title":"从分数得到类别分布","caption":"指数变换后按总和归一化","note":"计算示例使用分数 [1, 2, 3]，输出概率之和为 1。","url":"/diagrams/1/57.svg","sourceElements":[]}},{"page":58,"part":"ppt/slides/slide58.xml","text":["Multi-Layer Perceptron","Activation Functions","ReLU","Sigmoid","Softmax","• Sparse Activation","• Solving Vanishing Gradient","• Dying Neurons","• Smooth Function","• Vanishing Gradient","• Binary Classification","• Exponential Function","• Probability Distribution","• Multi-class classification","ReLU","Sigmoid","Softmax","• Sparse Activation","• Solving Vanishing Gradient","• Dying Neurons","• Smooth Function","• Vanishing Gradient","• Binary Classification","• Exponential Function","• Probability Distribution","• Multi-class classification"],"pictures":0,"hidden":false,"media":[],"links":[],"figure":{"page":58,"kind":"table","title":"激活函数的选择","caption":"把输出形式、梯度特性与使用位置联系起来","note":"","url":"/diagrams/1/58.svg","sourceElements":[]}},{"page":59,"part":"ppt/slides/slide59.xml","text":["Multi-Layer Perceptron","Activation Functions","Other functions:"],"pictures":1,"hidden":false,"media":[],"links":[],"figure":{"page":59,"kind":"activation","title":"其他非线性函数","caption":"通过响应曲线理解不同激活设计","note":"以双曲正切为例，观察零中心输出与两端饱和。","url":"/diagrams/1/59.svg","sourceElements":[]}},{"page":60,"part":"ppt/slides/slide60.xml","text":["Multi-Layer Perceptron","Summary: an example","Suppose we want to predict the commute time into city center.","﻿Define the loss function:","Find the parameters that can minimize this objective?"],"pictures":3,"hidden":true,"media":[],"links":[],"figure":{"page":60,"kind":"forward","title":"把各层组合成一个函数","caption":"先明确每层的形状，再沿箭头计算","note":"前向传播使用当前参数；训练决定参数如何改变。","url":"/diagrams/1/60.svg","sourceElements":[]}},{"page":61,"part":"ppt/slides/slide61.xml","text":["Multi-Layer Perceptron","Summary: An Example","﻿Compute the partial derivative:","﻿Gradient Decent:"],"pictures":2,"hidden":true,"media":[],"links":[],"figure":{"page":61,"kind":"forward","title":"把各层组合成一个函数","caption":"先明确每层的形状，再沿箭头计算","note":"前向传播使用当前参数；训练决定参数如何改变。","url":"/diagrams/1/61.svg","sourceElements":[]}},{"page":62,"part":"ppt/slides/slide62.xml","text":["Multi-Layer Perceptron","Summary: An Example","What other variables would be useful?","Distance to city center,","Day of the week,","Transportation,","etc.","Represent the day as 1-7","Represent the Transportation type as: Bus : 1, Bike : 2, Car: 3"],"pictures":4,"hidden":true,"media":[],"links":[],"figure":{"page":62,"kind":"forward","title":"把各层组合成一个函数","caption":"先明确每层的形状，再沿箭头计算","note":"前向传播使用当前参数；训练决定参数如何改变。","url":"/diagrams/1/62.svg","sourceElements":[]}},{"page":63,"part":"ppt/slides/slide63.xml","text":["Multi-Layer Perceptron","Summary: An Example","Fitting Non-Linear Model","linear model is too limited, right?","Maybe not, the key is really how to design features."],"pictures":3,"hidden":true,"media":[],"links":[],"figure":{"page":63,"kind":"forward","title":"把各层组合成一个函数","caption":"先明确每层的形状，再沿箭头计算","note":"前向传播使用当前参数；训练决定参数如何改变。","url":"/diagrams/1/63.svg","sourceElements":[]}},{"page":64,"part":"ppt/slides/slide64.xml","text":["Multi-Layer Perceptron","Summary: An Example","Fitting Non-Linear Model","Still linear model, just design some better features."],"pictures":3,"hidden":true,"media":[],"links":[],"figure":{"page":64,"kind":"forward","title":"把各层组合成一个函数","caption":"先明确每层的形状，再沿箭头计算","note":"前向传播使用当前参数；训练决定参数如何改变。","url":"/diagrams/1/64.svg","sourceElements":[]}},{"page":65,"part":"ppt/slides/slide65.xml","text":["Multi-Layer Perceptron","Summary: An Example","Fitting MLPs: ","Can we learn “good” features from data automatically?\t","Yes ! Multi-layer Perceptrons (MLPs) :","Define loss function:","GD with derivatives (Back Propagation)"],"pictures":3,"hidden":true,"media":[],"links":[],"figure":{"page":65,"kind":"forward","title":"把各层组合成一个函数","caption":"先明确每层的形状，再沿箭头计算","note":"前向传播使用当前参数；训练决定参数如何改变。","url":"/diagrams/1/65.svg","sourceElements":[]}},{"page":66,"part":"ppt/slides/slide66.xml","text":["Contents","Introduction & Overview","Multi-Layer Perceptron","﻿Training Neural Networks","Case Analysis"],"pictures":3,"hidden":false,"media":[],"links":[],"figure":{"page":66,"kind":"roadmap","title":"训练神经网络","caption":"围绕目标、梯度、更新与泛化组织训练过程","note":"","url":"/diagrams/1/66.svg","sourceElements":[]}},{"page":67,"part":"ppt/slides/slide67.xml","text":["Training Neural Networks","Problem Restatement","Given the training data .","Given the neural networks  with parameters  and loss functions .","Compute the empirical risk to approximate the expected risk:","Minimizing the empirical loss leads to an optimization problem:  ","How to solve this optimization problem?"],"pictures":2,"hidden":false,"media":[],"links":[],"figure":{"page":67,"kind":"training","title":"训练的闭环","caption":"由预测误差产生更新信号","note":"模型、损失和优化器共同决定参数如何从数据中学习。","url":"/diagrams/1/67.svg","sourceElements":[]}},{"page":68,"part":"ppt/slides/slide68.xml","text":["Training Neural Networks","Preliminary: Matrix Calculus ","The partial derivative of a scalar  with respect to a vector:","The partial derivative of a vector  with respect to a vector:"],"pictures":2,"hidden":false,"media":[],"links":[],"figure":{"page":68,"kind":"chain","title":"链式法则与矩阵求导","caption":"把整体导数拆成沿计算路径的局部导数","note":"多条路径影响同一变量时，需要累加各路径的梯度贡献。","url":"/diagrams/1/68.svg","sourceElements":[]}},{"page":69,"part":"ppt/slides/slide69.xml","text":["Training Neural Networks","Preliminary: Chain Rules"],"pictures":3,"hidden":false,"media":[],"links":[],"figure":{"page":69,"kind":"chain","title":"链式法则与矩阵求导","caption":"把整体导数拆成沿计算路径的局部导数","note":"多条路径影响同一变量时，需要累加各路径的梯度贡献。","url":"/diagrams/1/69.svg","sourceElements":[]}},{"page":70,"part":"ppt/slides/slide70.xml","text":["Training Neural Networks","Preliminary: Gradient Descent","Following negative gradient direction of a function ensures the fastest decrease in the function value.","By computing the derivative of the empirical risk ℛ with respect to the learnable parameters 𝑊, we can determine the update direction for the parameters."],"pictures":2,"hidden":false,"media":[],"links":[],"figure":{"page":70,"kind":"descent","title":"梯度下降的方向与步长","caption":"沿损失减小的局部方向更新参数","note":"曲线使用 L(θ)=θ²/2；箭头为该示例的实际梯度更新。","url":"/diagrams/1/70.svg","sourceElements":[]}},{"page":71,"part":"ppt/slides/slide71.xml","text":["Training Neural Networks","Training MLPs","Linear Regression didn’t work","What about MLPs?"],"pictures":3,"hidden":true,"media":[],"links":[],"figure":{"page":71,"