lides/slide98.xml","text":["Training Neural Networks","Overfitting & Underfitting"],"pictures":1,"hidden":false,"media":[],"links":[],"figure":{"page":98,"kind":"fit","title":"欠拟合与过拟合","caption":"表示能力与泛化需要同时考虑","note":"示意曲线用于比较拟合程度，不代表实际实验测量。","url":"/diagrams/1/98.svg","sourceElements":[]}},{"page":99,"part":"ppt/slides/slide99.xml","text":["Training Neural Networks","Overfitting & Underfitting","Underfitting: poor performance on both training and test set.","Overfitting: poor performance on test set while excellent performance on training set","• Model is too simple ","e.g., linear model for nonlinear data","• Inadequate training","e.g., too few iterations ","• Complicate the structure","• Increase training iterations","Solution","• Model is too complex ","e.g., Using high-order models to fit low-order functions","• Training data is insufficient","Solution","• Simplify the structure","• Regularization "],"pictures":2,"hidden":false,"media":[],"links":[],"figure":{"page":99,"kind":"fit","title":"欠拟合与过拟合","caption":"表示能力与泛化需要同时考虑","note":"示意曲线用于比较拟合程度，不代表实际实验测量。","url":"/diagrams/1/99.svg","sourceElements":[]}},{"page":100,"part":"ppt/slides/slide100.xml","text":["Training Neural Networks","Regularization","L1 Regularization ","contour lines of the loss function","contour lines of the L1 norm","Objective function   ","L1 Regularization ","https://www.zhihu.com/question/38081976/answer/2330394725"],"pictures":1,"hidden":false,"media":[],"links":["https://www.zhihu.com/question/38081976/answer/2330394725"],"figure":{"page":100,"kind":"regularization","title":"L1 与 L2 正则化","caption":"比较参数约束的几何形状","note":"L1 倾向产生稀疏解；L2 倾向连续地收缩权重。","url":"/diagrams/1/100.svg","sourceElements":[]}},{"page":101,"part":"ppt/slides/slide101.xml","text":["Training Neural Networks","Regularization","L2 Regularization ","contour lines of the loss function","contour lines of the L2 norm","Objective function   ","L2 Regularization "],"pictures":1,"hidden":false,"media":[],"links":[],"figure":{"page":101,"kind":"regularization","title":"L1 与 L2 正则化","caption":"比较参数约束的几何形状","note":"L1 倾向产生稀疏解；L2 倾向连续地收缩权重。","url":"/diagrams/1/101.svg","sourceElements":[]}},{"page":102,"part":"ppt/slides/slide102.xml","text":["Training Neural Networks","Regularization","L1 Regularization","• Sparsity","Intersects the loss contour at \"corners,\" forcing some weights to zero.","Tends to shrink some weights to zero","• Not differentiable at zero","L2 Regularization","• Density","Hypersphere has no conner, so it likely to touch contours away from the axes.","Shrinks weights uniformly but very unlikely to zero","• Smooth & differentiable"],"pictures":2,"hidden":false,"media":[],"links":[],"figure":{"page":102,"kind":"regularization","title":"L1 与 L2 正则化","caption":"比较参数约束的几何形状","note":"L1 倾向产生稀疏解；L2 倾向连续地收缩权重。","url":"/diagrams/1/102.svg","sourceElements":[]}},{"page":103,"part":"ppt/slides/slide103.xml","text":["Training Neural Networks","Regularization","Dropout","At each training epoch, neurons have a certain probability of being dropped out.","The network cannot rely too heavily on any single feature, forcing it to learn robust, distributed representations.","Any feature has a certain probability of being masked out"],"pictures":1,"hidden":false,"media":[],"links":[],"figure":{"page":103,"kind":"dropout","title":"Dropout：训练时随机屏蔽激活","caption":"模型不能始终依赖某一个固定单元","note":"被屏蔽的是本次计算中的激活；下次迭代可以采用不同掩码。","url":"/diagrams/1/103.svg","sourceElements":[]}},{"page":104,"part":"ppt/slides/slide104.xml","text":["Training Neural Networks","Regularization","Early Stopping","Training accuracy: may increase monotonically ","Test accuracy: might initially increase but start decreasing after reaching a certain threshold."],"pictures":1,"hidden":false,"media":[],"links":[],"figure":{"page":104,"kind":"early-stop","title":"依据验证表现选择停止点","caption":"训练误差和泛化误差可能呈现不同走势","note":"示意曲线用于说明早停；最终测试集不参与轮次选择。","url":"/diagrams/1/104.svg","sourceElements":[]}},{"page":105,"part":"ppt/slides/slide105.xml","text":["Training Neural Networks","Regularization","Data Augmentation","Insufficient data cause overfitting","Data augmentation to increase data diversity","original image","affine, shear, rotate, flip, blur, color transform ..."],"pictures":2,"hidden":false,"media":[],"links":[],"figure":{"page":105,"kind":"augment","title":"数据增强扩展可见变化","caption":"让标签保持有效的变换参与训练","note":"增强必须与任务兼容，不能随意改变应当预测的标签。","url":"/diagrams/1/105.svg","sourceElements":[{"url":"/diagrams/elements/1/image268.jpeg","lesson":1,"page":105}]}},{"page":106,"part":"ppt/slides/slide106.xml","text":["Training Neural Networks","Optimizer: BGD, SGD, Mini-Batch GD","The data used to compute the gradient at each parameter update","Batch Gradient Descent (BGD)","Stochastic Gradient Descent (SGD)","Mini-batch Gradient Descent (Mini-batch GD)"],"pictures":0,"hidden":false,"media":[],"links":[],"figure":{"page":106,"kind":"batch","title":"一次更新使用多少样本","caption":"全批量、单样本和小批量采用不同的梯度估计","note":"更新频率、吞吐量和梯度波动需要一起比较。","url":"/diagrams/1/106.svg","sourceElements":[]}},{"page":107,"part":"ppt/slides/slide107.xml","text":["Training Neural Networks","Optimizer: BGD, SGD, Mini-Batch GD","Method","BGD","SGD","Mini-batch GD","Data Used per Update","Entire training dataset","Single random sample","Small batch (e.g., 32, 64)","Characteristics","• Stable convergence","• High computational cost per update","• Slow and memory-intensive for large datasets","• Fast per iteration","• Unstable convergence","• High variance due to the noise","• Balances BGD and SGD","• Commonly used"],"pictures":0,"hidden":false,"media":[],"links":[],"figure":{"page":107,"kind":"batch","title":"一次更新使用多少样本","caption":"全批量、单样本和小批量采用不同的梯度估计","note":"更新频率、吞吐量和梯度波动需要一起比较。","url":"/diagrams/1/107.svg","sourceElements":[]}},{"page":108,"part":"ppt/slides/slide108.xml","text":["Training Neural Networks","Optimizer","The training data used in each iteration is typically a small batch.","The update direction to exhibit jagged or even random oscillations","How to teach the model “memories” the historical gradients?"],"pictures":1,"hidden":false,"media":[],"links":[],"figure":{"page":108,"kind":"branches","title":"优化算法的两个方向","caption":"利用历史方向，或根据历史尺度调整步长","note":"","url":"/diagrams/1/108.svg","sourceElements":[]}},{"page":109,"part":"ppt/slides/slide109.xml","text":["Training Neural Networks","Preliminary: Exponentially Weighted Average (EMA)","Given a sequence, calculate the average:","Key formula of EMA:","current observations","older observations","Decay rate, higher decay rate means smoother but slower adaptation"],"pictures":0,"hidden":false,"media":[],"links":[],"figure":{"page":109,"kind":"ema","title":"指数移动平均","caption":"新的统计量由历史状态与当前观测共同决定","note":"β 越大，历史信息的衰减通常越慢。","url":"/diagrams/1/109.svg","sourceElements":[]}},{"page":110,"part":"ppt/slides/slide110.xml","text":["Training Neural Networks","Optimizer: Momentum","Momentum enhances gradient descent by accumulating historical gradients to accelerate convergence and dampen oscillations.","historical gradients","current gradients","SGD","SGD with Momentum","https://www.cnblogs.com/froml77/p/14956375.html"],"pictures":3,"hidden":false,"media":[],"links":["https://www.cnblogs.com/froml77/p/14956375.html"],"figure":{"page":110,"kind":"optimizer","title":"优化器的更新路径","caption":"在同一个二次目标上观察不同更新规则","note":"轨迹为教学示例，目标 L(x,y)=(x²+10y²)/2；不能据此判定通用优劣。","url":"/diagrams/1/110.svg","sourceElements":[]}},{"page":111,"part":"ppt/slides/slide111.xml","text":["Training Neural Networks","Optimizer: Nesterov Acceleration","Momentum is not smart enough to predict possible future scenarios.","Approximately predict future weights"],"pictures":1,"hidden":false,"media":[],"links":[],"figure":{"page":111,"kind":"optimizer","title":"优化器的更新路径","caption":"在同一个二次目标上观察不同更新规则","note":"轨迹为教学示例，目标 L(x,y)=(x²+10y²)/2；不能据此判定通用优劣。","url":"/diagrams/1/111.svg","sourceElements":[]}},{"page":112,"part":"ppt/slides/slide112.xml","text":["Training Neural Networks","Optimizer: Adagrad","Adagrad is an adaptive gradient optimizer that uses different learning rates for different parameters based on the update frequency. For each parameter:"," is a diagonal matrix:","The overall formula is:"],"pictures":0,"hidden":false,"media":[],"links":[],"figure":{"page":112,"kind":"optimizer","title":"优化器的更新路径","caption":"在同一个二次目标上观察不同更新规则","note":"轨迹为教学示例，目标 L(x,y)=(x²+10y²)/2；不能据此判定通用优劣。","url":"/diagrams/1/112.svg","sourceElements":[]}},{"page":113,"part":"ppt/slides/slide113.xml","text":["Training Neural Networks","Optimizer: Adadelta & RMSprop","Adadelta is an extended algorithm of Adagrad to handle the problem of monotonically decreasing Adagrad learning rate.","Accumulation of squared gradients:","The step size of each weight update is as follows:","The exponentially weighted average is also used to calculate the root mean square of the step length:"],"pictures":0,"hidden":false,"media":[],"links":[],"figure":{"page":113,"kind":"optimizer","title":"优化器的更新路径","caption":"在同一个二次目标上观察不同更新规则","note":"轨迹为教学示例，目标 L(x,y)=(x²+10y²)/2；不能据此判定通用优劣。","url":"/diagrams/1/113.svg","sourceElements":[]}},{"page":114,"part":"ppt/slides/slide114.xml","text":["Training Neural Networks","Optimizer: Adadelta & RMSprop","The final Adadelta weight update formula is:","Adadelta does not even require a specified learning rate. The idea of ​​RMSprop is roughly the same, and its update formula is as follows:"],"pictures":0,"hidden":false,"media":[],"links":[],"figure":{"page":114,"kind":"optimizer","title":"优化器的更新路径","caption":"在同一个二次目标上观察不同更新规则","note":"轨迹为教学示例，目标 L(x,y)=(x²+10y²)/2；不能据此判定通用优劣。","url":"/diagrams/1/114.svg","sourceElements":[]}},{"page":115,"part":"ppt/slides/slide115.xml","text":["Training Neural Networks","Optimizer: Adam","Adaptive Moment Estimation is a bit like a combination of Momentum and RMSProp. First, an exponentially weighted average is applied to the gradient and the square of the gradient:","Then perform bias correction:","The final weight update formula is as follows:"],"pictures":0,"hidden":false,"media":[],"links":[],"figure":{"page":115,"kind":"optimizer","title":"优化器的更新路径","caption":"在同一个二次目标上观察不同更新规则","note":"轨迹为教学示例，目标 L(x,y)=(x²+10y²)/2；不能据此判定通用优劣。","url":"/diagrams/1/115.svg","sourceElements":[]}},{"page":116,"part":"ppt/slides/slide116.xml","text":["Training Neural Networks","Optimizer: AdamW","AdamW believes that Adam is not used correctly for weight decay. When we use L2 regularization, a square term of the weight is added after the loss:","When differentiating the loss function, the weight decay term appears in the gradient:","Therefore, the parameter update formula of the Adam optimizer is"],"pictures":0,"hidden":false,"media":[],"links":[],"figure":{"page":116,"kind":"optimizer","title":"优化器的更新路径","caption":"在同一个二次目标上观察不同更新规则","note":"轨迹为教学示例，目标 L(x,y)=(x²+10y²)/2；不能据此判定通用优劣。","url":"/diagrams/1/116.svg","sourceElements":[]}},{"page":117,"part":"ppt/slides/slide117.xml","text":["Training Neural Networks","Optimizer","Visualization diagrams of several optimizers:"],"pictures":2,"hidden":false,"media":[{"url":"/materials/1/media/image282.gif","type":"animation"},{"url":"/materials/1/media/image283.gif","type":"animation"}],"links":[],"figure":{"page":117,"kind":"optimizer","title":"优化器的更新路径","caption":"在同一个二次目标上观察不同更新规则","note":"轨迹为教学示例，目标 L(x,y)=(x²+10y²)/2；不能据此判定通用优劣。","url":"/diagrams/1/117.svg","sourceElements":[]}},{"page":118,"part":"ppt/slides/slide118.xml","text":["Training Neural Networks","Initialization","Avoid vanishing/exploding gradients in deep networks.","Enable faster convergence during training.","Ensure neurons start with diverse, non-zero activations.","Why Initialization?"],"pictures":1,"hidden":false,"media":[],"links":["https://www.cnblogs.com/PythonLearner/p/13173560.html"],"figure":{"page":118,"kind":"initialization","title":"初始化与信号尺度","caption":"过小或过大的初始尺度会随层数累积","note":"随机化打破神经元对称性；方差控制帮助稳定前向与反向信号。","url":"/diagrams/1/118.svg","sourceElements":[]}},{"page":119,"part":"ppt/slides/slide119.xml","text":["Training Neural Networks","Initialization","Avoid vanishing/exploding gradients in deep networks.","Enable faster convergence during training.","Ensure neurons start with diverse, non-zero activations."],"pictures":4,"hidden":true,"media":[],"links":["https://www.cnblogs.com/PythonLearner/p/13173560.html"],"figure":{"page":119,"kind":"initialization","title":"初始化与信号尺度","caption":"过小或过大的初始尺度会随层数累积","note":"随机化打破神经元对称性；方差控制帮助稳定前向与反向信号。","url":"/diagrams/1/119.svg","sourceElements":[]}},{"page":120,"part":"ppt/slides/slide120.xml","text":["Training Neural Networks","Initialization","Sample weights from a uniform distribution  or normal distribution ","Xavier Initialization (Linear activation function)","He Initialization (Considering ReLU)"],"pictures":0,"hidden":false,"media":[],"links":["https://zhuanlan.zhihu.com/p/40175178"],"figure":{"page":120,"kind":"initialization","title":"初始化与信号尺度","caption":"过小或过大的初始尺度会随层数累积","note":"随机化打破神经元对称性；方差控制帮助稳定前向与反向信号。","url":"/diagrams/1/120.svg","sourceElements":[]}},{"page":121,"part":"ppt/slides/slide121.xml","text":["Training Neural Networks","Xavier Initialization (Linear activation function)"],"pictures":1,"hidden":false,"media":[],"links":["https://zhuanlan.zhihu.com/p/40175178"],"figure":{"page":121,"kind":"variance","title":"Xavier 初始化的方差关系","caption":"把输入维度、权重方差和输出方差联系起来","note":"推导依赖独立性、零均值等近似条件；不同激活需要相应调整。","url":"/diagrams/1/121.svg","sourceElements":[]}},{"page":122,"part":"ppt/slides/slide122.xml","text":["Training Neural Networks","Xavier Initialization (Linear activation function)"],"pictures":1,"hidden":false,"media":[],"links":["https://zhuanlan.zhihu.com/p/40175178"],"figure":{"page":122,"kind":"variance","title":"Xavier 初始化的方差关系","caption":"把输入维度、权重方差和输出方差联系起来","note":"推导依赖独立性、零均值等近似条件；不同激活需要相应调整。","url":"/diagrams/1/122.svg","sourceElements":[]}},{"page":123,"part":"ppt/slides/slide123.xml","text":["Training Neural Networks","Xavier Initialization (Linear activation function)"],"pictures":1,"hidden":false,"m